Description: seaf-gc.sh: use this packaging's fixed FHS paths, drop pro/sqlite
 branches, check systemd units instead of process names, require the seafile
 identity
 Same TOPDIR-detection problem as reset-admin.sh (see reset-admin-fhs-paths.patch);
 sources /etc/seafile/seafile.env instead. validate_already_running now checks
 systemctl unit state (seafile.service, seafile-fileserver.service,
 seahub.service, seafile-fuse.service) instead of pgrep'ing process names, since
 seafdav runs embedded in seahub's gunicorn workers here rather than as its own
 process like in upstream's own layout. Drops check_python_executable (nothing
 here is python) and the IS_PRO_VERSION branch (community edition only).
 Re-execs as the seafile user via runuser when invoked as anyone else, before
 doing anything: this writes into the object store, and running as root would
 leave files owned by root that seafile.service can no longer manage.
Author: dionysius <dragon.dionysius@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Comment: install-layout specific, not something upstream's own tar.gz/docker install needs.
